  "description": "FELNES crystallizes in the cubic crystal system with space group I -4 3 d. Reported CIF formula moiety: C118 H86 Nd6 O36 S9. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1D (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2D (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd1H (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2H (Nd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.750-5.279 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 85.72-146.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Nd6(μ6-CO3)(L)6(LH)3(H2O)5(OH)]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
